    1	"""
    2	S185 (verify-15 of S169): cluster-boundary k_* probe.
    3	
    4	Adversarial test: the 21% spike-block fraction in S169/S183 is computed
    5	at k_* extrapolated linearly from S82's three-point fit. Is this k_*
    6	choice structurally privileged, or only one of many reasonable k_*
    7	selections each giving a different fraction?
    8	
    9	We compute the spike block / pi(N) ratio at MULTIPLE k_* selection rules
    10	applied to the same SVD data:
    11	
    12	    R0  S82-extrapolated (the canonical S169/S183 choice)
    13	    R1  Marchenko-Pastur upper edge: k_* = #{sigma_k > 2*sqrt(M*p_N)}
    14	    R2  Spectral elbow: k_* = argmax_k of (sigma_k - sigma_{k+1})/sigma_k
    15	    R3  Largest plateau-end gap: k_* at the deepest gap below k <= 2*M^{1/2}
    16	    R4  Sector-completion (cumulative phi(q) up to small primes)
    17	
    18	If the 21% asymptote is a real structural fact, its value should be
    19	similar across these rules. If it depends on the canonical k_* choice,
    20	the spread reveals model-dependence.
